From 070e7710da00d7a0a8889f6c532cabbdea10b603 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:15:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netstack: IPv6 addresses, neighbor discovery and SLAAC

smoltcp skips NDP and SLAAC on an IP medium, so the Ethernet link does them
itself, like ARP: it answers neighbor solicitations for its addresses,
resolves IPv6 next hops with solicitations to the solicited-node group,
maps IPv6 multicast to 33:33 MACs, sends router solicitations and takes a
/64 prefix with the autonomous flag from router advertisements (modified
EUI-64 address, RFC 4862). Smolnetd copies the link-local address, the
SLAAC address and the router into the interface and the route table
(fe80::/64, ff00::/8, the prefix, ::/0 via the router), plus ::1 on the
loopback device. The router sends IPv6 packets with the source address
smoltcp chose. No duplicate address detection, no lifetimes beyond zero,
no IPv6 sockets in relibc yet.
